    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "bargauge",
      "title": "stage mean latency against its budget allocation",
      "description": "Bar length is that stage's exact mean (histogram sum/count) as a fraction of its allocation in BUDGET (benchmark/replay.py): plan 5, embed 120, cache.lookup 25, retrieve 60, fuse 5, rerank 1200, generate 2000 ms. Orange at 80% of the allocation, red at 100%. WHY THE MEAN AND NOT p95, when the budget is written in p95: the fixed buckets in tracing.py (0.005 … 0.25, 0.5, 1.0, 2.5, 5.0 s) cannot resolve these allocations. The smallest bucket is 5 ms, so plan and fuse — whose true p50 is ~0.05 ms and ~0.01 ms — both report a p95 of 4.75 ms and would sit permanently at 95% of a 5 ms allocation. Measured in one live window: rerank p95 read 2425 ms against an exact mean of 1787 ms, embed p95 read 800 ms against an exact mean of 149 ms. So this panel shows the number the histogram can state exactly, and the p95 check stays where it is exact: PYTHONPATH=. python -m benchmark.replay --n 30. Read it accordingly — a mean over the allocation is unambiguously bad, a mean under it is not proof of p95 compliance. The one-line fix for the panel: add 0.9, 1.2, 2.0, 3.5 to _LATENCY_BUCKETS_S. generate is absent without an API key.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 6
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
